@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 2, 2026</p>

    <p>
        Pony Up Performance respects your privacy and is committed to protecting
        the personal information you provide when using our website and services.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>
        We may collect information you provide directly to us, including your name,
        email address, account information, vehicle information, and information
        entered while using Pony Up Performance tools and services.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you choose to sign in using an external provider such as Google
        or Facebook, we may receive basic account information authorized by
        you through that provider, such as your name, email address, and
        provider user identifier.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>

    <p>We may use collected information to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Create and maintain your Pony Up Performance account.</li>
        <li>Authenticate your identity when you sign in.</li>
        <li>Provide vehicle analysis and other requested services.</li>
        <li>Maintain and improve our website, applications, and services.</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, and unauthorized access.</li>
        <li>Communicate with you regarding your account or services.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>External Sign-In Data</h2>

    <p>
        Pony Up Performance uses information received through supported external
        sign-in providers for authentication, account creation, account linking,
        and functionality associated with your Pony Up Performance account.
    </p>

    <p>
        We do not sell external sign-in data or personal information to advertisers
        or other third parties.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

    <p>
        We may share information with service providers when necessary to operate
        Pony Up Performance, including hosting, database, authentication, and
        payment-processing services. These providers are only given information
        necessary to perform their services.
    </p>

    <p>
        We may also disclose information when required by law or when reasonably
        necessary to protect our users, business, or services.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
        We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary
        to provide our services, maintain accounts, meet legal obligations, resolve
        disputes, and enforce agreements.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        Users may request deletion of personal information associated with their
        Pony Up Performance account. Instructions are available on the
        <a asp-page="/DataDeletion">User Data Deletion page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>

    <p>
        We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards designed to
        protect personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure,
        alteration, or destruction.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>
        Pony Up Performance may use third-party services such as Facebook,
        payment processors, hosting providers, and other technology providers.
        Their handling of information is governed by their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy as our services evolve. Updates will be
        posted on this page with a revised effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact and Privacy Requests</h2>

    <p>
        Questions, privacy requests, and data deletion requests may be submitted
        through the contact options provided on the Pony Up Performance website.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Pony Up Performance</strong><br />
        Website: ponyupperformance.com
    </p>
</div>
